License, in source or object form, excluding Third-Party Components.
"Modified Software" means any modification of, or work based on, the
Software that You make. References in this License to the Software include
Modified Software, but never include Third-Party Components themselves,
even when combined with the Software.

"Third-Party Components" means the specific files identified by path in
the NOTICE file, or bearing a notice in the file itself, as licensed under
terms other than this License, in each case only to the extent of the work
of the third-party author. A directory-level or package-level entry in the
NOTICE file identifies only files that originate from the named
third-party work. All other files made available by Licensor, including
model, world, mesh, image and asset files authored by Licensor, are
Software even if they are located in the same directory or package as a
Third-Party Component.

"Your Works" means applications, tools, models, worlds, curricula,
notebooks, scripts and similar works that You create for use with Genuine
PhysiCar Products or the PhysiCar Platform, even if they use the Software's
interfaces, templates or examples or include incidental portions of the
Software that Licensor provides for that purpose. Your Works are not
Software.

"Genuine PhysiCar Product" means a physical robot, vehicle, controller
board or other hardware device that is manufactured by or for Licensor and
is sold or supplied as a PhysiCar product by Licensor or by a distributor
authorized in writing by Licensor, as identified by a serial number,
purchase record, the list of Genuine PhysiCar Products published at
physicar.ai/legal, or other means Licensor uses to identify genuine units.
A Genuine PhysiCar Product does not cease to be genuine because its owner
repairs it or replaces failed or worn parts with equivalent parts.
Authorization of a distributor does not by itself make any product a
Genuine PhysiCar Product. Software images, factory-reset or recovery
images, installers, containers, virtual machines and development
environments (including hosted or cloud development environments), and the
PhysiCar Platform, are not Genuine PhysiCar Products; to the extent they
contain the Software they are Software and are subject to this License.

"Non-Genuine Hardware" means any robot, vehicle, drone, controller board,
single-board computer or other device that runs the Software to operate or
control physical motors, actuators or sensors, or that is intended or
advertised to do so, and that is not a Genuine PhysiCar Product. A
general-purpose computer, virtual machine, container or cloud environment
that runs the Software only for simulation, development, testing, study or
teaching, and that does not control a physical robot other than a Genuine
PhysiCar Product, is not Non-Genuine Hardware.

"PhysiCar Platform" means the PhysiCar AI online services operated by
Licensor at physicar.ai and its subdomains, or any successor services.

"Permitted Purpose" means each of the following:
  (a) use, study, research, evaluation and experimentation, by an
      individual or by a school, university or other non-profit
      institution, that is not for direct or indirect commercial
      advantage, on any computer or server under Your control. Receiving
      a public research grant, or publishing results, is not by itself a
      commercial advantage;
  (b) education, instruction, training and competitions, whether or not a
      fee is charged to participants, in which each participant uses the
      Software on a Genuine PhysiCar Product or through the PhysiCar
      Platform. In connection with such an activity the Software
      (including any simulator) may also be installed and run on
      computers and servers under the control of the organizer, the
      instructors and the participants, for preparation, for the activity
      itself and for follow-up work, where that running is ancillary to
      the use of Genuine PhysiCar Products or the PhysiCar Platform and
      not a substitute for it;
  (c) installing, running, modifying, extending, repairing and operating
      the Software on a Genuine PhysiCar Product that You own or lawfully
      control, on the PhysiCar Platform, or on any computer or server
      under Your control for a purpose described in (a), (b), (d) or (e);
  (d) developing, testing and sharing Your Works and Modified Software
      that are designed for use with Genuine PhysiCar Products or the
      PhysiCar Platform and not for operating, controlling or simulating
      Non-Genuine Hardware;
  (e) evaluation by any person or entity, on computers under its control,
      for the purpose of deciding whether to acquire Genuine PhysiCar
      Products or PhysiCar Platform services; and
  (f) submitting Contributions to Licensor.
An act described in Section 3 is not a Permitted Purpose. No Permitted
Purpose includes installing or running the Software on, or using it to
operate or control, Non-Genuine Hardware.

"Competing Offering" means a product or service that is marketed, offered
or provided as an alternative to, or that performs substantially the same
function as, a Genuine PhysiCar Product or the PhysiCar Platform, including
an educational or hobby robot, a robot kit or board, a robot software image
for Non-Genuine Hardware, a robotics simulator, or a hosted robotics or AI
simulation, training or education platform. A Competing Offering does not
include (i) education, instruction, training or competitions that You
provide within Permitted Purpose (b), whether or not a fee is charged,
merely because participants could obtain similar instruction or tools from
the PhysiCar Platform; (ii) hosting permitted by Section 3(b); or (iii)
Your Works and Modified Software that You Distribute in compliance with
Section 2 solely for use on Genuine PhysiCar Products or with the PhysiCar
Platform. These exclusions do not extend to any robot, kit, board, software
image, simulator or online platform that You provide as a substitute for a
Genuine PhysiCar Product or the PhysiCar Platform, even if it is used in
education.

"Distribute" means to make the Software available to any third party, in
source or object form, by any means, including sale, gift, lease,
download, network transfer or pre-installation on hardware. Providing
access to a running instance of the Software over a network is not
Distribution; it is governed by Section 3(b).

"Contribution" means any work of authorship that You intentionally submit
to Licensor for inclusion in the Software.

"You" means the individual or legal entity exercising rights under this
License. If You are a legal entity, You are responsible for ensuring that
entities You control comply with this License with respect to Software
they receive through You, and an act by such an entity in connection with
that Software is treated as Your act.

