3. RESTRICTIONS

The license granted in Section 2 is subject to the following
restrictions. These restrictions apply notwithstanding Section 2 and
regardless of whether an act would otherwise fall within a Permitted
Purpose. Unless You hold a separate written commercial license from
Licensor, You may not:

  (a) Distribute, sell, lease or otherwise provide the Software, or any
      product, kit, board, software image, container or environment
      containing the Software, for use on or with Non-Genuine Hardware, or
      install or run the Software on Non-Genuine Hardware;

  (b) provide the Software, or any of its functionality, to third parties
      as a hosted, managed, cloud or network service, or as
      software-as-a-service; except that You may run the Software on
      infrastructure You control and make it available over a network to
      persons taking part in an activity that You conduct within a
      Permitted Purpose (including Your students, employees, members,
      trainees, competition or hackathon participants, and visitors to an
      event), provided that (i) access is limited to those persons and is
      not offered to the general public, (ii) the hosted Software is not
      offered, marketed or priced as a separate product or service
      (tuition, course, event or participation fees are not fees for the
      Software), and (iii) You do not host the Software for, or on behalf
      of, another organization's business;

  (c) copy, adapt or incorporate the Software, in whole or in part, into a
      Competing Offering; use the Software to design, develop, operate or
      provide a Competing Offering; or use the Software or its outputs to
      train a machine-learning model for a Competing Offering;

  (d) remove, alter or obscure any copyright, license, trademark or
      attribution notice contained in the Software;

  (e) sublicense the Software, or Distribute the Software under any terms
      other than this License (this does not apply to Your Works);

  (f) use the Software to (i) gain unauthorized access to the PhysiCar
      Platform, or to a Genuine PhysiCar Product that You do not own or
      lawfully control; (ii) evade, falsify or interfere with the fees,
      credits, quotas, license verification or genuine-product
      verification of the PhysiCar Platform; (iii) cause a device that is
      not a Genuine PhysiCar Product to identify itself to the PhysiCar
      Platform as a Genuine PhysiCar Product; or (iv) access the PhysiCar
      Platform other than through its documented interfaces or through the
      Software as provided by Licensor; or

  (g) make, market, sell, supply or Distribute any hardware, kit, board,
      disk image, installer, script, configuration or instructions that
      are designed, adapted or advertised for installing or running the
      Software on Non-Genuine Hardware, or knowingly induce, encourage or
      assist any other person to do anything described in Section 3(a) or
      this Section 3(g).

Section 3(c) does not prohibit (i) evaluating, reviewing, testing or
comparing the Software or Genuine PhysiCar Products with other products or
services, and publishing or reporting the results, where this is done for
a Permitted Purpose and not for the purpose of designing, developing,
training or improving a Competing Offering; or (ii) using the general
knowledge, skills and experience that You gain from using the Software,
provided that the Software's source code, architecture or specific
implementation is not used, reproduced or adapted for a Competing
Offering.

The following are not breaches of Section 3(f) when done to a Genuine
PhysiCar Product that You own or lawfully control, for a Permitted
Purpose: configuring, pinning, delaying, disabling or redirecting its
update mechanism (including to a mirror You operate); changing or
resetting its local passwords or access controls; and modifying its
parameters or software. You remain responsible for safe operation as
stated in Section 10.

